;; Reviewed 2026-10-08 (written by Claude, from the design, the MACRO
;; manual and the VAX's listing; for the user's review). Why this is
;; right:
;; - a[i] := F(j): the target's index is in R0 when F is called, so it is
;;   moved up to R2, which F's mask saves, and the result stored to
;;   A[R2] (section 7, as for any value in R0 or R1).
;; - m[i, F(j)] := m[F(i), j]: the row's address moves from R0 to R2 for
;;   the first call; the second index, F's result, is checked, then moves
;;   from R0 to R3 for the second call, so the target is (R2)[R3] and the
;;   value (R0)[R1]: four registers, none spilled, since a register that
;;   is a base or an index cannot be in the frame. F's results are
;;   widened in place (CVTWL R0, R0) before they are checked.
;; - CASE a[i]: the selector is moved to a slot of the frame, -4(FP), and
;;   compared there, so that no register stays in use across the arms.
;; - FOR i := 0 TO a[j]: the limit is evaluated once, after i := 0, and
;;   kept in the frame (Oberon2.pdf 9.8); a[i] := i in the body checks i
;;   on every pass.
;; - WHILE (a[i] < a[j]) & b[i]: a[i], the left operand, is evaluated
;;   first (R1 then R0 would be the other order); b[i] is moved to a
;;   register for BLBS, whose operand is a longword.
;; - s[i] := s[j] + {i}: {i} is ASHL i, #1 (section 8), then one BISL3
;;   of two indexed operands into a third.
;; - POC_TRAP, outside the module, is named in general mode, G^ (section
;;   7, decided with the user 2026-10-06), which the linker makes
;;   relative or absolute as the symbol is relocatable or absolute (MACRO
;;   5.2.5), so that a routine in a shareable image is reached too
;;   ("always use general addressing mode for any external reference",
;;   Linker 4.2).
;; - Step 8 (decided 2026-10-08) adds the module's key, POC_K1_ and its
;;   .sym's key, a global symbol its importers declare .EXTERNAL, and, as
;;   it is the program's main module, the program's start,
;;   VAXINDEXREGISTERS_MAIN, which calls the initializer, returns
;;   SS$_NORMAL and is named by .END.
